{"files": [{"id": 39864117, "name": "00085472can171904-sup-185422_2_supp_4436440_p0l4rs.xls", "size": 2987520, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/39864117", "supplied_md5": "ed79605f05dca219c42224dcf3aaa4f5", "computed_md5": "ed79605f05dca219c42224dcf3aaa4f5", "mimetype": "application/vnd.ms-excel"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 1456447, "full_name": "Hideki Terai", "first_name": "Hideki", "last_name": "Terai", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 2357803, "full_name": "Shunsuke Kitajima", "first_name": "Shunsuke", "last_name": "Kitajima", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14930454, "full_name": "Danielle S. Potter", "first_name": "Danielle S.", "last_name": "Potter", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 2047393, "full_name": "Yusuke Matsui", "first_name": "Yusuke", "last_name": "Matsui", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14930457, "full_name": "Laura Gutierrez Quiceno", "first_name": "Laura Gutierrez", "last_name": "Quiceno", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 15205, "full_name": "Ting Chen", "first_name": "Ting", "last_name": "Chen", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Ting_Chen", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14930460, "full_name": "Tae-jung Kim", "first_name": "Tae-jung", "last_name": "Kim", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 6789302, "full_name": "Maria Rusan", "first_name": "Maria", "last_name": "Rusan", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14930463, "full_name": "Tran C. Thai", "first_name": "Tran C.", "last_name": "Thai", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 773276, "full_name": "Federica Piccioni", "first_name": "Federica", "last_name": "Piccioni", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 5136575, "full_name": "Katherine A. Donovan", "first_name": "Katherine A.", "last_name": "Donovan", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1276038, "full_name": "Nicholas Kwiatkowski", "first_name": "Nicholas", "last_name": "Kwiatkowski", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 6490874, "full_name": "Kunihiko Hinohara", "first_name": "Kunihiko", "last_name": "Hinohara", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 79839, "full_name": "Guo Wei", "first_name": "Guo", "last_name": "Wei", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Guo_Wei", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 150685, "full_name": "Nathanael S. Gray", "first_name": "Nathanael S.", "last_name": "Gray", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 5136572, "full_name": "Eric S. Fischer", "first_name": "Eric S.", "last_name": "Fischer", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 165223, "full_name": "Kwok-Kin Wong", "first_name": "Kwok-Kin", "last_name": "Wong", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 133856, "full_name": "Teppei Shimamura", "first_name": "Teppei", "last_name": "Shimamura", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1335960, "full_name": "Anthony Letai", "first_name": "Anthony", "last_name": "Letai", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 218409, "full_name": "Peter S. Hammerman", "first_name": "Peter S.", "last_name": "Hammerman", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 9341861, "full_name": "David A. Barbie", "first_name": "David A.", "last_name": "Barbie", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [{"name": "ARTICLE ABSTRACT", "value": "An increasingly recognized component of resistance to tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKI) involves persistence of a drug-tolerant subpopulation of cancer cells that survive despite effective eradication of the majority of the cell population. Multiple groups have demonstrated that these drug-tolerant persister cells undergo transcriptional adaptation via an epigenetic state change that promotes cell survival. Because this mode of TKI drug tolerance appears to involve transcriptional addiction to specific genes and pathways, we hypothesized that systematic functional screening of EGFR TKI/transcriptional inhibitor combination therapy would yield important mechanistic insights and alternative drug escape pathways. We therefore performed a genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 enhancer/suppressor screen in EGFR-dependent lung cancer PC9 cells treated with erlotinib + THZ1 (CDK7/12 inhibitor) combination therapy, a combination previously shown to suppress drug-tolerant cells in this setting. As expected, suppression of multiple genes associated with transcriptional complexes (EP300, CREBBP, and MED1) enhanced erlotinib/THZ1 synergy. Unexpectedly, we uncovered nearly every component of the recently described ufmylation pathway in the synergy suppressor group. Loss of ufmylation did not affect canonical downstream EGFR signaling. Instead, absence of this pathway triggered a protective unfolded protein response associated with STING upregulation, promoting protumorigenic inflammatory signaling but also unique dependence on Bcl-xL. These data reveal that dysregulation of ufmylation and ER stress comprise a previously unrecognized TKI drug tolerance pathway that engages survival signaling, with potentially important therapeutic implications.Significance: These findings reveal a novel function of the recently described ufmylation pathway, an ER stress survival signaling in drug-tolerant persister cells, which has important biological and therapeutic implications. Cancer Res; 78(4); 1044\u201357. \u00a92017 AACR.", "settings": {"validations": {"min_length": 10, "max_length": 10000}, "placeholder": "ARTICLE ABSTRACT"}, "field_type": "textarea", "order": null, "is_mandatory": false}], "figshare_url": "https://aacr.figshare.com/articles/dataset/Supplementary_Table_S2_from_ER_Stress_Signaling_Promotes_the_Survival_of_Cancer_Persister_Cells_Tolerant_to_EGFR_Tyrosine_Kinase_Inhibitors/22418004", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>Result of GSEA analysis</p>", "funding": "NCI", "funding_list": [{"id": 335318, "title": "NCI", "grant_code": "", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 1}, {"id": 23225166, "title": "the Schaubert, Gloria T. Maheu, and Heerwagen Family Funds for Lung Cancer Research", "grant_code": "", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 1}, {"id": 23225169, "title": "Lilly oncology", "grant_code": "", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 1}], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 2987520, "created_date": "2023-03-31T01:27:56Z", "modified_date": "2024-02-21T11:30:11Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 52, "name": "CC BY", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["Chemotherapy", "Combination chemotherapy", "Drug Resistance", "Novel mechanisms", "Regulation of gene expression in drug resistance", "Gene Regulation", "Posttranscriptional and translational control", "Hematological Cancers", "Lung Cancer"], "keywords": ["Chemotherapy", "Combination chemotherapy", "Drug Resistance", "Novel mechanisms", "Regulation of gene expression in drug resistance", "Gene Regulation", "Posttranscriptional and translational control", "Hematological Cancers", "Lung Cancer"], "categories": [{"id": 37339, "title": "Cancer", "parent_id": 0, "path": "/37339", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 106}, {"id": 37354, "title": "Molecular and Cellular Biology", "parent_id": 0, "path": "/37354", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 106}, {"id": 37360, "title": "Therapeutic Research and Development", "parent_id": 0, "path": "/37360", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 106}], "references": ["https://doi.org/10.1158/0008-5472.CAN-17-1904"], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "Terai, Hideki; Kitajima, Shunsuke; Potter, Danielle S.; Matsui, Yusuke; Quiceno, Laura Gutierrez; Chen, Ting; et al. (2018). Supplementary Table S2 from ER Stress Signaling Promotes the Survival of Cancer \u201cPersister Cells\u201d Tolerant to EGFR Tyrosine Kinase Inhibitors. American Association for Cancer Research. Dataset. https://doi.org/10.1158/0008-5472.22418004.v1", "related_materials": [{"id": 44916677, "identifier": "10.1158/0008-5472.CAN-17-1904", "title": "ER Stress Signaling Promotes the Survival of Cancer \u201cPersister Cells\u201d Tolerant to EGFR Tyrosine Kinase Inhibitors", "relation": "IsSupplementTo", "identifier_type": "DOI", "is_linkout": true, "link": "https://doi.org/10.1158/0008-5472.CAN-17-1904"}], "is_embargoed": false, "embargo_date": null, "embargo_type": null, "embargo_title": "", "embargo_reason": "", "embargo_options": [], "id": 22418004, "title": "Supplementary Table S2 from ER Stress Signaling Promotes the Survival of Cancer \u201cPersister Cells\u201d Tolerant to EGFR Tyrosine Kinase Inhibitors", "doi": "10.1158/0008-5472.22418004.v1", "handle": "", "url": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/22418004", "published_date": "2023-03-31T01:27:56Z", "thumb": "", "defined_type": 3, "defined_type_name": "dataset", "group_id": 46225, "url_private_api": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/account/articles/22418004", "url_public_api": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/22418004", "url_private_html": "https://figshare.com/account/articles/22418004", "url_public_html": "https://aacr.figshare.com/articles/dataset/Supplementary_Table_S2_from_ER_Stress_Signaling_Promotes_the_Survival_of_Cancer_Persister_Cells_Tolerant_to_EGFR_Tyrosine_Kinase_Inhibitors/22418004", "timeline": {"posted": "2023-03-31T01:27:56", "publisherPublication": "2018-02-15T00:00:00", "firstOnline": "2023-03-31"}, "resource_title": "ER Stress Signaling Promotes the Survival of Cancer \u201cPersister Cells\u201d Tolerant to EGFR Tyrosine Kinase Inhibitors", "resource_doi": "10.1158/0008-5472.CAN-17-1904"}